) and identified 557 peptides unique to the LRCAGE proteome. These results highlight that the usage of LRCAGE in building the custom proteome database enables the identification of novel proteins not only in H1299 cells but also in CPTAC LUAD samples.
Next, we investigated antigens that were uniquely detected by the LRCAGE proteome. First, using antigens predicted by NetMHC (
